\paragraph{Execution Simulation and Verification.}
Code World Models~\cite{meta2025cwm} predict output strings via 32B mid-training on execution traces; extensions address step-by-step prediction~\cite{maimon2026selfexecution}, code reasoning~\cite{liu2024codemind}, simulation-execution bridging~\cite{lee2026solidcoder}, and failure mode analysis~\cite{abdollahi2025demystifying}. Alternative formulations include trajectory-level reward models~\cite{shum2025swerm}, chain-of-thought verification~\cite{xu2025patchreasoner}, per-test classifiers~\cite{ni2023lever,chen2023codet}, and learned quality metrics~\cite{zhuo2024icescore,dong2024codescore,zhou2023codebertscore}. Test-time scaling~\cite{snell2024scaling,li2025sstar,chen2025vgsearch} and self-consistency~\cite{wang2023selfconsistency} further demonstrate verification value. None compare formulations at controlled capacity.

\paragraph{Process vs.\ Outcome Supervision.}
Lightman et al.~\cite{lightman2023letsverify} and Uesato et al.~\cite{uesato2022solving} show process-level verification outperforms outcome-level for mathematical reasoning; DreamPRM-Code~\cite{dreamprm2025code} and PRL-Coder~\cite{ye2025prlcoder} apply this to code. Our per-test classification is structurally analogous; TOST equivalence ($p = 0.007$) confirms per-test matches trajectory-level accuracy with additional diagnostic value.

\paragraph{Repair, Mutation Testing, and Task Framing.}
CodeRL~\cite{le2022coderl}, AlphaCode~\cite{li2022alphacode,alphacode2023team}, and Reflexion~\cite{shinn2023reflexion} use execution feedback for iterative improvement. SWE-bench~\cite{jimenez2024swebench,chowdhury2024swebenchverified} provides standard benchmarks; SWE-agent~\cite{yang2024sweagent} and Agentless~\cite{xia2024agentless} demonstrate repair pipelines where verification is a persistent bottleneck~\cite{yang2025aprsurvey}. Predictive mutation testing~\cite{tufano2019predictive,kim2022predictive,wang2024llmmutation,jain2023contextual} shares our per-test structure. LoRA~\cite{hu2022lora} and QLoRA~\cite{dettmers2024qlora} enable parameter-efficient fine-tuning; DeepSeek-Coder~\cite{guo2024deepseekcoder} preserves pretrained understanding. Task framing~\cite{raffel2020t5,lewis2020bart,rajpurkar2016squad} affects model performance; we extend this lens to code verification, finding complexity moderates the tradeoff.

